.TH "NOTMUCH-DUMP" "1" "Apr 17, 2026" "0.40" "notmuch"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
notmuch-dump \- creates a plain-text dump of the tags of each message
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
\fBnotmuch\fP \fBdump\fP [\-\-gzip] [\-\-format=(batch\-tag|sup)] [\-\-output=<\fIfile\fP>] [\-\-] [<\fIsearch\-term\fP> ...]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Dump tags for messages matching the given search terms.
.sp
Output is to the given filename, if any, or to stdout.
.sp
These tags are the only data in the notmuch database that can\(aqt be
recreated from the messages themselves. The output of notmuch dump is
therefore the only critical thing to backup (and much more friendly to
incremental backup than the native database files.)
.sp
See notmuch\-search\-terms \%<#\:notmuch-search-terms-7> for details of the supported syntax
for <search\-terms>. With no search terms, a dump of all messages in
the database will be generated. A \fB\-\-\fP argument instructs notmuch that
the remaining arguments are search terms.
.sp
Supported options for \fBdump\fP include
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-gzip
Compress the output in a format compatible with \fBgzip(1) \%<https://\:manpages\:.debian\:.org/\:gzip\:.1\:.html>\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-format=(sup|batch\-tag)
Notmuch restore supports two plain text dump formats, both with
one message\-id per line, followed by a list of tags.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B batch\-tag
The default \fBbatch\-tag\fP dump format is intended to more
robust against malformed message\-ids and tags containing
whitespace or non\-\fBascii(7) \%<https://\:manpages\:.debian\:.org/\:ascii\:.7\:.html>\fP characters. Each line
has the form:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
+<*encoded\-tag*\e > +<*encoded\-tag*\e > ... \-\- id:<*quoted\-message\-id*\e >
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Tags are hex\-encoded by replacing every byte not matching the
regex \fB[A\-Za\-z0\-9@=.,_+\-]\fP with \fB%nn\fP where nn is the two
digit hex encoding. The message ID is a valid Xapian query,
quoted using Xapian boolean term quoting rules: if the ID
contains whitespace or a close paren or starts with a double
quote, it must be enclosed in double quotes and double quotes
inside the ID must be doubled. The astute reader will notice
this is a special case of the batch input format for
notmuch\-tag \%<#\:notmuch-tag-1>; note that the single message\-id query is
mandatory for notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1>\&.
.TP
.B sup
The \fBsup\fP dump file format is specifically chosen to be
compatible with the format of files produced by
\fBsup\-dump(1) \%<https://\:manpages\:.debian\:.org/\:sup-dump\:.1\:.html>\fP\&. So if you\(aqve previously been using sup
for mail, then the notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1> command provides
you a way to import all of your tags (or labels as sup calls
them). Each line has the following form:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
<*message\-id*\e > **(** <*tag*\e > ... **)**
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
with zero or more tags are separated by spaces. Note that
(malformed) message\-ids may contain arbitrary non\-null
characters. Note also that tags with spaces will not be
correctly restored with this format.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-include=(config|properties|tags)
Control what kind of metadata is included in the output.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B config
Output configuration data stored in the database. Each line
starts with \(dq#@ \(dq, followed by a space separated key\-value
pair.  Both key and value are hex encoded if needed.
.TP
.B properties
Output per\-message (key,value) metadata.  Each line starts
with \(dq#= \(dq, followed by a message id, and a space separated
list of key=value pairs.  Ids, keys and values are hex encoded
if needed.  See notmuch\-properties \%<#\:notmuch-properties-7> for more details.
.TP
.B tags
Output per\-message boolean metadata, namely tags. See \fIformat\fP above
for description of the output.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The default is to include all available types of data.  The option
can be specified multiple times to select some subset. As of
version 3 of the dump format, there is a header line of the
following form:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
#notmuch\-dump <*format*>:<*version*> <*included*>
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
where <\fIincluded\fP> is a comma separated list of the above options.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-output=<filename>
Write output to given file instead of stdout.
.UNINDENT
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
notmuch \%<#\:notmuch-1>,
notmuch\-config \%<#\:notmuch-config-1>,
notmuch\-count \%<#\:notmuch-count-1>,
notmuch\-hooks \%<#\:notmuch-hooks-5>,
notmuch\-insert \%<#\:notmuch-insert-1>,
notmuch\-new \%<#\:notmuch-new-1>,
notmuch\-properties \%<#\:notmuch-properties-7>,
notmuch\-reply \%<#\:notmuch-reply-1>,
notmuch\-restore \%<#\:notmuch-restore-1>,
notmuch\-search \%<#\:notmuch-search-1>,
notmuch\-search\-terms \%<#\:notmuch-search-terms-7>,
notmuch\-show \%<#\:notmuch-show-1>,
notmuch\-tag \%<#\:notmuch-tag-1>
